{:id "flymake"
 :author "hkjels"
 :title "Catch the small mistakes early"
 :command "flymake-show-buffer-diagnostics"
 :tip? true
 :tags #{:built-in :diagnostics :development :eglot}
 :description "See buffer diagnostics without leaving Emacs."
 :code "(use-package flymake\n  :ensure nil\n  :hook (emacs-lisp-mode . flymake-mode))"
 :language "elisp"
 :url "https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/flymake.html"
 :body ["Flymake displays diagnostics supplied by the current mode or another backend. The example enables the built-in Emacs Lisp backend; it does not assume that a checker is available for every programming language."
        "Run M-x flymake-show-buffer-diagnostics for a list, or use flymake-goto-next-error and flymake-goto-prev-error to move between findings."
        "Eglot already enables Flymake in buffers it manages. You do not need a second hook for those buffers, and other languages may need an appropriate backend or external checker."]}
